---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import TitleComponent from "../components/misc/TitleComponent.astro";
import SeparatorComponent from "../components/misc/SeparatorComponent.astro";
---

<Layout>
    <TitleComponent Titulo="SpaceX Website Privacy Policy" />
    <SeparatorComponent />
    <!-- MAIN -->
    <main class="pb-20 px-5 mx-10 font-jost">
        <div class="mb-5">
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mt-1">Last updated: April 1, 2024</p>
        </div>
        <p class="mb-6">
            We don’t knowingly sell your personal information, but we still have to tell you what we collect from you and how we use it. We may update this policy from time to time. Your continued use of this site indicates your agreement to the updated terms.
        </p>
        <p>
            If you are a prospective, current or past Starlink customer, this Privacy Policy does not apply to you—please refer instead to our Starlink Privacy Policy.
        </p>
        <br>
        <h2 class="font-medium">1. What Personal Information Do We Collect?</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc mx-10">
            <li><strong>Identity Data:</strong> first name, last name, title.</li>
            <li><strong>Contact Data:</strong> postal address, email address, telephone numbers.</li>
            <li><strong>Profile Data:</strong> username, password, purchases, customer service requests.</li>
            <li><strong>Financial Data:</strong> payment card details, billing address.</li>
            <li><strong>Transaction Data:</strong> payments and purchase details.</li>
            <li><strong>Technical Data:</strong> IP address, browser info, location, OS, platform, website interactions.</li>
            <li><strong>Communication Data:</strong> preferences, uploaded files, inferences from other data.</li>
            <li><strong>Employment Data:</strong> if applying for a job with SpaceX, including work history, education, contact info.</li>
        </ul>
        <br>
        <h2 class="font-medium">2. How Do We Collect Personal Information?</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc mx-10">
            <li><strong>Directly from You:</strong> account registration, product/service requests, subscriptions, correspondence.</li>
            <li><strong>From Third Parties:</strong> service providers, subcontractors, search providers, prior employment data.</li>
            <li><strong>Cookies & Online Tracking:</strong> cookies, server logs, device identifiers; for logged-in and non-logged-in users. More info at <a href="https://www.Cookiepro.com" class="underline text-blue-600">CookiePro</a>.</li>
        </ul>
        <br>
        <p class="font-medium">3. How and Why Do We Use Personal Information?</p>
        <ul class="list-disc mx-10">
            <li>Provide goods and services</li>
            <li>Process and deliver orders</li>
            <li>Manage payments, fees, and charges</li>
            <li>Manage our relationship with you</li>
            <li>Protect our business, detect fraud, enforce policies</li>
            <li>Comply with legal obligations</li>
            <li>Deliver relevant news and offers</li>
            <li>Assess employment applications</li>
        </ul>
        <br>
        <h2 class="font-medium">4. With Whom Do We Disclose Personal Information?</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc mx-10">
            <li><strong>Service Providers:</strong> affiliates, analytics, hosting, backup, customer service.</li>
            <li><strong>Government & Advisors:</strong> regulators, courts, professional advisors.</li>
            <li><strong>Business Transfers:</strong> mergers, acquisitions, reorganizations.</li>
            <li>Third parties with your consent.</li>
        </ul>
        <br>
        <h2 class="font-medium">5. How Do We Protect Personal Information?</h2>
        <p>
            We implement technological, physical, and administrative measures to protect your data. While we strive for security, no method is perfect and we cannot guarantee complete protection.
        </p>
        <br>
        <h2 class="font-medium">6. Your Privacy Rights</h2>
        <p>
            You may have rights to access, update, or erase your data. For US residents, review our US State Privacy Notice. For EEA+ residents, review the EEA+ Privacy Notice. Opt-out instructions via <a href="mailto:privacy@spacex.com" class="underline text-blue-600">privacy@spacex.com</a>.
        </p>
        <br>
        <h2 class="font-medium">7. Children’s Privacy</h2>
        <p>
            We do not knowingly collect data from children under 16. If you are a parent/guardian and believe your child submitted data, contact us at <a href="mailto:privacy@spacex.com" class="underline text-blue-600">privacy@spacex.com</a>.
        </p>
        <br>
        <h2 class="font-medium">8. Data Retention</h2>
        <p>We retain personal information only as long as necessary or required by law.</p>
        <br>
        <h2 class="font-medium">9. Third-Party Websites</h2>
        <p>
            We are not responsible for third-party websites linked from ours. Their policies may differ, and your data may be handled differently.
        </p>
        <br>
        <h2 class="font-medium">10. Contact Us</h2>
        <p><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:privacy@spacex.com" class="underline text-blue-600">privacy@spacex.com</a></p>
        <p><strong>Postal Mail:</strong> Space Exploration Technologies Corp., Attn: Privacy/Legal, 1 Rocket Road, Hawthorne, CA 90250</p>
    </main>
</Layout>